Description: manage iPhones, files and local backups
 A native GTK 4 / libadwaita application for inspecting iOS devices and
 iTunes/Finder backups on Linux.
 .
 It lists connected devices through usbmuxd, creates backups with live
 progress and cancellation, unlocks encrypted backups, browses their
 contents (photos, videos, music, documents, contacts, messages, call
 history, notes and calendar), previews and exports files, writes files to
 the device, restores a backup to its device, and resets a device to
 factory settings after an explicit typed confirmation.
 .
 Backups are only read. A connected device is written to only after an
 explicit user action.
 .
 The application is a self-contained build: it carries its own CPython
 runtime and Python libraries under /usr/lib/device-dock/app and does not
 use the system Python, so it keeps working when a distribution upgrades
 its default Python version.
 .
 Dependencies: the Depends list contains the system libraries and tools
 needed for every feature the application offers, including the GTK 4 and
 libadwaita typelibs, live phone browsing (ifuse, fuse3, usbmuxd) and
 audio/video playback (GStreamer). The Recommends list contains optional
 extras that only improve previews and diagnostics; the application
 reports the missing tool instead of failing when one is absent.
 .
